    "narrative": "Our primary offensive engine today centers on **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who boasts the day\u2019s highest efficiency score (81.36). With a favorable matchup against the left-handed Peralta, the boost provided by the opponent\u2019s slow delivery\u2014which optimizes his stolen base environment\u2014makes **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** a must-start staple. He is joined in the top tier by **Brendan Donovan** (68.26) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (68.02). **Brendan Donovan** benefits significantly from the leadoff spot against Wesneski, while **Jung Hoo Lee** leverages a strong wind-out projection and a high-leverage SP matchup to maximize his utility. **Gleyber Torres** also earns a strong recommendation (67.46) as he slots into the leadoff role against Kay, capitalizing on a strong platoon advantage to anchor the utility spot.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal field, specifically selecting between **Lawrence Butler** (49.30) and the bench option **JJ Bleday** (48.77). While **Lawrence Butler** faces a tough southpaw in Gore, his park factors provided just enough of a cushion to nudge him ahead of **JJ Bleday**. The optimizer ultimately sidelined **JJ Bleday** not only due to a lower raw efficiency score but also because of a looming 39% rain risk that introduces unnecessary variance for a bench asset. We are also keeping a close eye on **Masyn Winn** and **Luis Arraez**; despite their middling scores, their roles within the lineup keep them inside the starting frame, though they remain the first candidates to be pulled if we need to preserve game caps later in the week.\n\nOwners should remain vigilant regarding the volatile environment for our outfielders facing Mackenzie Gore today. While **Zack Gelof** (60.96) is well-positioned thanks to park factors and a high-probability SB environment, both he and **Lawrence Butler** are swinging against a pitcher who could dictate a low-scoring affair. Conversely, the platoon edge for **Daulton Varsho** (56.02) remains a statistical positive against Hancock, despite a slight park penalty. We are currently holding **Yainer Diaz** and **Justin Crawford** in reserve, as both are out of today's lineup, leaving our catching depth solely to **Cal Raleigh** (61.74), who remains a solid play despite being buried in the #7 spot.",
